    <section class="content-section shell" id="guide" aria-labelledby="guide-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><span class="section-kicker">A little advice goes a long way</span><h2 id="guide-title">How to make the judges remember you.</h2></div>
        <p>You don't need the fanciest tech. You need a clear problem, a working idea, and a story people can follow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-grid">
        <article class="guide-card"><h3>Start with a real problem</h3><p>Talk to someone who has it. Show the judges why solving it matters before showing your slides.</p></article>
        <article class="guide-card"><h3>Build one thing well</h3><p>Keep the scope small. A working core feature beats a long list of promises every time.</p></article>
        <article class="guide-card"><h3>Show, don't just tell</h3><p>Prepare a live demo and a backup recording. Make the benefit clear in your first minute.</p></article>
        <article class="guide-card"><h3>Make every teammate count</h3><p>Share the work, practice your pitch, and make sure everyone can explain the solution.</p></article>
